    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "Hey, I've got a heifer that just came out of rumenotomy an hour ago. Can u give me a quick rundown of what i should be looking out for over the next few days regarding infection and when i can start getting her back on feed?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Watch for fever, lethargy, reduced appetite, or foul-smending drainage from the rumen or neck to detect early signs of infection or complications. You should generally start small amounts of small granular feed within 12 to 24 hours, gradually increasing the portion size over the next few days as her appetite improves. Ensure she does not graze on long-coarser feed for the first two weeks to prevent rumen wall irritation or tearing while healing.",
