      "content": "Subclinical issues like deep abscesses often require specific diagnostic tests like palpation, ultrasound, or ruminoscopy before you see outward symptoms. Look for subtle changes in rumen fluid consistency, sudden drops in body weight, or prolonged constipation despite good appetite, as these can indicate internal fluid accumulation or displacement. If you are unsure, consult with a veterinarian immediately early on rather than waiting for visible signs to develop.",
