      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The best approach is to establish a strict observation schedule focusing on daily changes in appetite, rumen fluid consistency, and body condition score before visible illnesses appear. Implementing a spaced sampling of rumen fluid or considering an ultrasound exam can help you catch fluid buildup, abscesses, or leaks from the needles before they escalate into severe infections. Keeping your initial feed very small and easily digestible minimizes the risk of triggering these hidden issues, giving your animal the best chance for a smooth recovery. If you notice any unexpected shift in behavior or stability, logging these details and reporting them immediately to a livestock vet will be crucial.",
